WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.610
- You are a mega mentor
on the voice this season.

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.030
Um, super stoked about that.

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.810
But I have to ask,

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:07.562
who is your favorite coach Ed?

00:00:07.562 --> 00:00:08.960
(audience cheers)

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:09.910
I mean, who is it?

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:10.750
Just shout it out.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:12.040
Just don't feel shy.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:12.873
- No Kelly, only one person.

00:00:12.873 --> 00:00:14.951
Only one person gave good gifts.

00:00:14.951 --> 00:00:16.672
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:16.672 --> 00:00:17.505
- It was, yeah.

00:00:17.505 --> 00:00:18.480
- You are like, I can't say.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.572
- It must have been you.

00:00:19.572 --> 00:00:22.130
Because I, actually I
still have the jacket.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.712
- You still see, I gave you presents.

00:00:23.712 --> 00:00:26.400
- I still have the jacket in this house.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.440
- I will buy your love Ed Sheeran.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.170
I will do it.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.810
Well, no, your daughter Lyra,

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.010
which is the most beautiful name ever.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.180
She just turned one.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.110
So how do you think,

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.110
we were talking about her
whenever you were visiting.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:39.020
'Cause it was your first time away

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.470
from her for that amount of time.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.760
So how do you think she's changed you?

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:43.680
- Well, I mean,

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.903
my bedtime has shifted from,

00:00:46.851 --> 00:00:49.080
I'm no longer going to bed at five.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:52.330
I'm getting up at four
or five, which is good.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:53.163
But no,

00:00:53.163 --> 00:00:54.280
I think there's like a different emotion

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:57.900
that has come through having a daughter.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.190
And, man, she's just wonderful.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.023
She's just wonderful.

00:01:01.023 --> 00:01:02.280
She's just started walking.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.910
She knows what her eyes and head

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:05.890
and mouth and blah, blah, blah.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.470
And she's on the verge of talking

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:08.303
and just,

00:01:08.303 --> 00:01:10.637
it's incredible to watch
all these things happen.

